            "date": "2022-03-23T21:53:05Z"
          },
          "message": "Fix Go 1.18 Test Generation, Enable Go 1.18 Tests, Disable Some Tests That Are Broken In Go 1.18\n\nSummary:\nGo 1.18 breaks our test generation code, because the signature of [[ https://pkg.go.dev/testing#MainStart | testing.MainStart ]] changed due to the addition of [[ https://go.dev/doc/fuzz/ | fuzzing ]].\n\nPreviously, we relied on using the same `test_main.go` generated file to run all our tests, and this was fine to use across different versions of Go. Now we need versioned versions of the `test_main.go` file since 1.16 and 1.18 have incompatible signatures for `testing.MainStart`.\n\nI just pass in an empty array for the new `fuzzTargets` argument, didn't actually implement it.\n\nThis diff also enables 1.18 tests.\n\nSome tests have been marked to only run in Go 1.16 because they are broken in Go 1.18:\n- //go/src/dropbox/blackbird/blackbird_jobs/data_governance/data_retention/itemdata_projector/scenarios_tests_group2:scenarios_tests_group2_test_1.18\n- //go/src/dropbox/devtools/image_builder/fasttrack:fasttrack_test_1.18\n- //go/src/dropbox/secretsauce/cert_monitor:cert_monitor_test_1.18\n- //go/src/dropbox/yaps/apiserver/statediff:statediff_test_1.18\n\nThis build has error logs for these tests: https://changes.pp.dropbox.com/commit_source/643e1b37c6b24253adf1294b3eb348e6/?buildID=6026ffead8c1401d88407fda076a29f5\n\nTest Plan: `arc test` and yolo. If any broken 1.18 tests slipped through the cracks, I'll disable them and skip the queue\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 98d0268a6b21d1f766659d5d99c791c3517707a8",
